"Ao Li - Homepage (https://lumos-leo.github.io/)\nciteturn31view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://lumos-leo.github.io/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 129\nL0: 【0†Image: Ao Li】\nL1: # Ao Li (李骜)\nL2: \nL3: I am currently a Lecturer at the College of Computer and Information Science, Chongqing Normal University (CQNU). My research focuses on low-level vision and efficient vision models, with a particular emphasis on image super-resolution. I am also interested in exploring how generative models and large multimodal models can contribute to this area.\nL4: Before joining CQNU, I received my Ph.D. degree from the University of Electronic Science and Technology of China (UESTC) in 2026, where I was jointly supervised by 【1†Prof. Le Zhang†scholar.google.com】 and 【2†Prof. Ce Zhu†scholar.google.com】. I received my M.Eng. degree from Chongqing University of Posts and Telecommunications in 2020 and my B.Eng. degree from Chongqing University in 2017.\nL5: Prior to my doctoral studies, I worked as a researcher at Sinovatio in 2021 and as a research assistant at UESTC in 2022.\nL6: Email: aoli.cq95@gmail.com / 【3†GitHub†github.com】 / 【4†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com】\nL7: \nL8: Open to collaboration Please feel free to contact me to discuss research ideas and potential projects.\nL9: \nL10: * * *\nL11: ## Preprints\nL12: \nL13:   1. Rarity-Aware Discrete Diffusion with Spatially Consistent Decoding for Photo-Realistic Image Super-Resolution\nL14: \nL15: Ao Li, Yapeng Du, Yi Xin, Lei Zhu, Le Zhang, Guangtao Zhai, Ce Zhu, Xiaohong Liu\nL16: \nL17: arXiv preprint, 2026. 【5†PDF†arxiv.org】\nL18: \nL19:   2. Deep unfolding network for hyperspectral image super-resolution with automatic exposure correction\nL20: \nL21: Yuan Fang, Yipeng Liu, Jie Chen, Zhen Long, Ao Li, Chong-Yung Chi, Ce Zhu\nL22: \nL23: arXiv preprint, 2024. 【6†PDF†arxiv.org】\nL24:   3. PASTA: Towards Flexible and Efficient HDR Imaging Via Progressiv